<h1>About</h1>
<p>A dream is born...</p>
<br>
<p>Alright fine, too heavy handed? </p>
<br>
<p>In all honesty, I don't know if this is going to work, but I sincerely hope it does.</p>
<br>
<p>
    A confluence of events led to the launch of this effort. I was sitting in the drive-thru of a well-known coffee chain that rhymes with barknucks, marveling at myself
    for paying more than $5 for a cold brew and listening to the latest debate about Student Loan Forgiveness on the radio when I not-so-casually thought,
    "Man, I'd definitely skip one cup of coffee a month to help pay off someone's student loan debt."
</p>
<br>
<p>
    From that moment, an idea started to form. I wanted to start a subscriber-based email list that costs $5 a month and minimize the
    number of emails sent to just one per month. That email would like the current "winner" of the drawing and state how many subscribers there were,
    so all members could see wher the money goes and how we could actually change lives.
</p>
<br>
<p>
    In the spirit of the Aha! moment, I set work on this version of the website. Think of it as a future-based, scholarship in-reverse...
</p>
<br>
<p>
    Will it work? Well...that's up to you, dear friends. I know what I think I would do if offered a chance to help cancel someone's debt; but I'm not sure
    how others will respond. Still, if even a small percentage of folks respond to this movement, I think we have a real shot at doing some good.
</p>
<br>
<p>
    If you still have questions or concerns, feel free to reach out to me directly. I'll do my best to answer all inquiries with speed and clarity.
    If I have time, I'll even offer to jump on a video chat or something. I love feedback and I'd love to hear what you think we can do to make this
    a better experience for everyone.
</p>

<h2>But <i>how</i> does it work?</h2>
<p>Using a service called <a href="https://plaid.com/">Plaid</a> we'll use the collected funds of our subscribers to make a payment directly to someone's student loan account. 
</p>
<p>No fishy business will be tolerated, and we won't ever just give someone a lump sum of cash. We don't aim to take on the lottery, after all.</p>
<p>The website and newsletter will be extremely lightweight to keep things simple and costs low so that collected funds go directly to the people who need it most!</p>
<p>So click that button, subscribe, and join a revolution!</p>
